        <h1>Privacy Policy</h1>
        <p class="legal-updated">Last updated: February 28, 2026</p>
      </div>

      <div class="legal-content">

        <section>
          <h2>1. Introduction</h2>
          <p>At GameLift, we take your privacy seriously. This Privacy Policy explains how we collect, use, store, and protect your personal information when you use our platform. By using GameLift, you consent to the data practices described in this policy.</p>
          <p>This policy complies with the General Data Protection Regulation (GDPR) of the European Union and the Organic Law on Data Protection and Digital Rights Guarantee (LOPDGDD) of Spain.</p>
        </section>

        <section>
          <h2>2. Data Controller</h2>
          <p>The data controller responsible for your personal data is:</p>
          <ul>
            <li><strong>Platform:</strong> GameLift</li>
            <li><strong>Contact Email:</strong> support@gamelift.com</li>
            <li><strong>Location:</strong> Las Palmas de Gran Canaria, Spain</li>
          </ul>
        </section>

        <section>
          <h2>3. Information We Collect</h2>

          <h3>3.1 Information You Provide</h3>
          <ul>
            <li><strong>Account Data:</strong> Username, email address, and password (encrypted) when you register.</li>
            <li><strong>Profile Data:</strong> Profile picture, bio, and social links you choose to add.</li>
            <li><strong>Content Data:</strong> Reviews, comments, reactions, collections, and library entries you create.</li>
            <li><strong>Developer Data:</strong> If you register as an indie developer, additional information related to your game projects.</li>
          </ul>

          <h3>3.2 Information Collected Automatically</h3>
          <ul>
            <li><strong>Usage Data:</strong> Pages visited, features used, timestamps of activity.</li>
            <li><strong>Session Data:</strong> Authentication tokens and session cookies necessary for maintaining your login state.</li>
            <li><strong>Device Data:</strong> Browser type and general device information for compatibility purposes.</li>
          </ul>

          <h3>3.3 Information from Third Parties</h3>
          <p>We receive game metadata (titles, covers, descriptions, ratings) from IGDB, game artwork from SteamGridDB, and price information from CheapShark. These services do not provide us with your personal data.</p>
        </section>

        <section>
          <h2>4. How We Use Your Information</h2>
          <p>We use your personal data for the following purposes:</p>
          <ul>
            <li><strong>Service Provision:</strong> To create and maintain your account, display your reviews, manage your library, and enable social features.</li>
            <li><strong>Notifications:</strong> To send you in-app notifications about reactions to your reviews, new comments, followers, and platform updates.</li>
            <li><strong>Community Features:</strong> To display your activity in the Community Pulse feed for users who follow you, and to enable social interactions.</li>
            <li><strong>Platform Improvement:</strong> To analyze usage patterns and improve the user experience.</li>
            <li><strong>Security:</strong> To protect against fraud, abuse, and unauthorized access, including CSRF protection and password recovery.</li>
            <li><strong>Communication:</strong> To send password reset emails and essential service notifications.</li>
          </ul>
        </section>

        <section>
          <h2>5. Legal Basis for Processing</h2>
          <p>Under GDPR, we process your data based on:</p>
          <ul>
            <li><strong>Consent:</strong> When you agree to these terms during registration.</li>
            <li><strong>Contractual Necessity:</strong> To provide the services you have requested (account management, reviews, library tracking).</li>
            <li><strong>Legitimate Interest:</strong> For platform security, fraud prevention, and service improvement.</li>
          </ul>
        </section>

        <section>
          <h2>6. Data Storage and Security</h2>
          <p>Your data is stored securely using the following measures:</p>
          <ul>
            <li><strong>Authentication:</strong> Managed by Firebase Authentication. Passwords are never stored in plain text and are handled exclusively by Firebase's secure infrastructure.</li>
            <li><strong>Database:</strong> User data, reviews, and content are stored in Google Cloud Firestore with encryption at rest and in transit.</li>
            <li><strong>Sessions:</strong> Authentication sessions use HTTP-only cookies that cannot be accessed by client-side scripts.</li>
            <li><strong>CSRF Protection:</strong> All form submissions and API requests are protected against Cross-Site Request Forgery attacks using double-submit cookie tokens.</li>
            <li><strong>Input Validation:</strong> All user inputs are validated and sanitized to prevent injection attacks.</li>
          </ul>
        </section>

        <section>
          <h2>7. Data Sharing</h2>
          <p>We do not sell, rent, or trade your personal information. Your data may be shared only in these circumstances:</p>
          <ul>
            <li><strong>Public Content:</strong> Reviews, comments, reactions, and profile information you choose to make public are visible to other users.</li>
            <li><strong>Service Providers:</strong> We use Firebase (Google) for authentication and data storage. Google processes this data under their own privacy policy and GDPR compliance measures.</li>
            <li><strong>Email Service:</strong> Password recovery emails are sent via Gmail SMTP. Only your email address is used for this purpose.</li>
            <li><strong>Legal Requirements:</strong> We may disclose information if required by law or in response to valid legal processes.</li>
          </ul>
        </section>

        <section>
          <h2>8. Your Rights (GDPR)</h2>
          <p>As a user in the European Union, you have the following rights:</p>
          <ul>
            <li><strong>Right of Access:</strong> Request a copy of all personal data we hold about you.</li>
            <li><strong>Right to Rectification:</strong> Correct inaccurate or incomplete personal data through your profile settings.</li>
            <li><strong>Right to Erasure:</strong> Request deletion of your account and personal data ("right to be forgotten").</li>
            <li><strong>Right to Restriction:</strong> Request that we limit processing of your data in certain circumstances.</li>
            <li><strong>Right to Portability:</strong> Receive your personal data in a structured, commonly used format.</li>
            <li><strong>Right to Object:</strong> Object to processing based on legitimate interests.</li>
            <li><strong>Right to Withdraw Consent:</strong> Withdraw your consent at any time by deleting your account.</li>
          </ul>
          <p>To exercise any of these rights, please contact us at <strong>support@gamelift.com</strong>. We will respond within 30 days.</p>
        </section>

        <section>
          <h2>9. Cookies</h2>
          <p>GameLift uses the following cookies:</p>
          <ul>
            <li><strong>Session Cookie:</strong> Essential cookie that maintains your login state. HTTP-only, expires after 1 hour.</li>
            <li><strong>CSRF Token:</strong> Security cookie used to prevent cross-site request forgery attacks.</li>
          </ul>
          <p>We do not use tracking cookies, advertising cookies, or analytics cookies from third parties. Our cookies are strictly necessary for the operation of the platform.</p>
        </section>

        <section>
          <h2>10. Data Retention</h2>
          <ul>
            <li><strong>Account Data:</strong> Retained as long as your account is active.</li>
            <li><strong>Reviews & Content:</strong> Retained as long as your account exists. Upon account deletion, all associated content will be removed.</li>
            <li><strong>Password Reset Tokens:</strong> Automatically expire after 1 hour and are deleted after use.</li>
            <li><strong>Activity Logs:</strong> Community Pulse activity data is retained for up to 90 days.</li>
          </ul>
        </section>

        <section>
          <h2>11. Children's Privacy</h2>
          <p>GameLift is not intended for children under the age of 16. We do not knowingly collect personal information from children under 16. If we become aware that a child under 16 has provided us with personal data, we will take steps to delete such information.</p>
        </section>

        <section>
          <h2>12. International Data Transfers</h2>
          <p>Your data may be processed in servers located outside the European Economic Area (EEA) through our use of Firebase (Google Cloud). Google provides adequate safeguards under Standard Contractual Clauses (SCCs) approved by the European Commission to ensure your data is protected in accordance with GDPR standards.</p>
        </section>

        <section>
          <h2>13. Changes to This Policy</h2>
          <p>We may update this Privacy Policy from time to time. Significant changes will be communicated through an in-app notification. We encourage you to review this page periodically. Your continued use of GameLift after changes constitutes acceptance of the updated policy.</p>
        </section>

        <section>
          <h2>14. Contact & Complaints</h2>
          <p>If you have questions or concerns about this Privacy Policy, contact us at:</p>
          <p><strong>Email:</strong> support@gamelift.com</p>
          <p>If you believe your data protection rights have been violated, you have the right to lodge a complaint with the Spanish Data Protection Agency (AEPD) at <strong>www.aepd.es</strong>.</p>
        </section>

